# LLM cost notes

Pricing is per million tokens, input and output priced separately; output is several times more expensive.

Rough per-request estimate for our agent: system prompt + tool definitions ≈ 3k tokens (cacheable), user request + observations ≈ 1–2k, output ≈ 300. With prompt caching the repeated prefix is billed at a fraction of the normal input price after the first call.

Budget rules we agreed:
- a monthly project cap, per-user daily caps, and a separate cap for examiners;
- every call is logged with tokens and cost;
- when a cap is reached the agent says so and runs nothing.

Things that blow the budget: sending whole files into the prompt, retry loops without a limit, and forgetting that each observation turn resends the whole conversation.
